    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 31.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.28"/> he betihtlod weorðę ⁊ he ut oðhleape, gilde se hlaford þæs mannes were ðam cingce.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf he betyhtlod weorðe, ⁊ he ut ætleape, gylde se hlaford ðæs mannes wér ðam cynge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif he betyhled weorðe ⁊ he ut hleape, gylde se hlaford þæs mannes were þam cyninge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi accusetur et fugiat, reddat dominus eius regi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.11"/> weram (id est pretium natiuitatis) hominis illius.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Si post<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.10"/> calumniam euaserit, dominus soluat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/> eius ƿere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.12"/> regi, et plegii quod calumniatus est. Si autem infra annum et unum diem dominus eius illum capere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.13"/> poterit, recipiat hoc quod pro eo dedit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi accusatus effugiat, soluat dominus illius regi redempcionem eius.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="31a.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="192" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf he betyhtlod weorðe ⁊ he ut ætleape<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_31-1.robnote.fn.6"/>, gylde se hlaford ðæs mannes wér ðam cynge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="272" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf he betihtlod weorðe and he ut oðhleape, gilde se hlaford þæs mannes were ðam cingce.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn er angeklagt wird, er jedoch hinaus entflieht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.de.1"/>, zahle der Herr dem König das Wergeld dieses Untergebenen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_31-1.lnote.de.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if he is accused but escapes, let the lord pay the king the wergild of that man.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#missing"/><pb n="193" ed="#robertson"/>And if he is accused and escapes, the lord shall pay his (the man's) wergeld to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="466" ed="#whitelock"/>And if he is accused and he escapes, the lord is to pay the man’s wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="273" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if he comes to be accused and escapes, the lord is to pay the fugitive’s wergild to the king.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="335"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-11">I Atr 1.11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1, 11</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_52-1">Leis Wl 52.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-11">I Atr 1.11–13</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 31:1-2: I Atr 1:11-13</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Atr 1.11.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 335, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 272, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “| man: hi B”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">oðhleape: ætleape B; leape A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">man: hi B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius r. r. illius <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius r. r. illius Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gih he betythled weorþ ⁊ he uthl., gylde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gih he betythled weorþ ⁊ he uthl., gylde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyning <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyning Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">primo <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">primo S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. s. <hi rend="italic">Cb Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. s. Cb Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. w. <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. w. Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">queat c. <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> c. p. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">queat c. instead of c. p. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 30, 7¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 30, 7¹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_31-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zusatz in Inst, dass Bürge[nverband?] Bestohlenem Ersatz schuldet, stammt vielleicht aus 30, 6; der Rückempfang des Wergeldes durch den Herrn, wenn dieser den Verbrecher binnen Jahr und Tag stellt, erinnert an III Eg 6, 2, wo der Bürge, was er statt des Verbrechers hatte zahlen müssen, in einem Jahr zurückerhält. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 3h. 5. 13e; zur Rückgabe <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Murdrum 15; zur Frist Jahr und Tag 1. 3. Letztere ist nicht Agsächsisch</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The addition in Inst, that the surety[-group?] owes compensation to the person robbed, perhaps comes from 30, 6; the lord’s recovery of the wergild if he produces the criminal within a year and a day recalls III Eg 6, 2, where the surety gets back within a year what he had had to pay in place of the criminal. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 3h. 5. 13e; on the restitution <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Murdrum 15; on the time limit Jahr und Tag 1. 3. The latter is not Anglo-Saxon</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_31-1.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><label>ætleape</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">oðhleape</hi> G, Ld; <hi rend="italic">hleape</hi> A.</seg></note>
      </div>
